DME is still being worked on at OSF.  General Availability of the
second component of DME, the Network Management Option (NMO) was announced
at the OSF members meeting in May.  Tapes of NMO will start shipping
in a week or so.  The NMO contains

	support for SNMP and CMIP protocols

	support for the X/Open Management API (XMP) 

	a event service (ESS) module processing SNMP traps and CMIP
	events

	a naming resolution service (NRS) providing X.500 naming

	a general purpose instrumentation request broker for 
	passing management data between protocol stacks (SNMP, CMIP), 
	processing modules (ESS, NRS), and the XMP library.

	The package developer kit for compiling GDMO definitions into
	XOM header files
	
	The metadata compiler and agent for building interface
	repository from GDMO object descriptions. 

The first component of DME, the DME Distributed Services, (license
management, event service, software distribution service, subsystem
management, and pc service) has been available from OSF since 
December 1993.  Several companies have licensed it and are developing
product plans based on the the technology.   

Discussions are underway among several companies for follow on
projects for DME using the new OSF PST process. (A PST project is
initiated by system vendors, ISVs, and/or end users and submitted to
OSF, contrasted with an RFT in which OSF initiates the project.) 

For printed DME  information contact direct@osf.org.
For general DME questions, contact me.

