Hello:

Is there a version of Encina that supports the MON_CONCURRENT_SHARED
scheduling policy for monitor application servers?  This policy allows
the Encina monitor to schedule concurrent threads within a processing 
agent of an application server.  This facility is posted with the info
pages for AIX 3.2.5.  Also, the option is available in the mon_handle.h
file but my version of Encina does not seem to support this option as 
a parameter to the mon_SetSchedulingPolicy call. I am running 
Encina 1.0.1 on top of AIX 3.2.5 on a set of RS/6000s.

So far, I have attempted using concurrent threads with the scheduling
policy MON_SHARED.  Since the MON_SHARED policy interleaves RPC
processing, whenever one of my threads (transactions) block the whole PA
blocks and all concurrent threads within the PA blocks.  I assume the
MON_CONCURRENT_SHARED scheduling policy overcomes this problem?  Is
there any other way of solving this problem without abandoning the TP
monitor altogether?

Your rapid, timely response is greatly appreciated.

Regards,
Dex
