We are developing a driver for a VME frame grabber  ( Imaging Technology
150/40 IMS ) under OSF/1 1.3, Alpha AXP 300/400 workstation
using the DEC VME - TurboChannel adapter. Using the T-6000 adapter
as the VME System Controller we are able to access the frame grabber
register space (located in the A16 VME address space). We can't either 
read or write the image memory (the base address is software selectable
in A24 or A32 address space). We performed also a test using a KAV-30
and the adapter (this time not as system controller), 
and we accessed successfully the KAV memory (A32 addressing mode). 
We noticed a strange fact: we were able to access  VME address range 
from FF000000 to FFFFFFFF on the KAV-30
using the switch default configuration (all zeros) while on the manuals 
this configuration should allow the access only to a A32 VME address
range from 0000000 - 007FFFFF.
We feel a trouble in accessing A24-A32 VME space onto the adapter,
or a mismatch in the supported documentation. 
We would like to get aware of known problems related to such behavior.
Any suggestion will be greatly appreciated.

